Fukuzawa looked startled and hurriedly let go of {f:my|my} hand.
She stared at {f:me|me}, dumbfounded, as if she were looking at something frightening.
"Sorry... I didn't mean to yell like that."{p}

"Well.
There weren't any problems as such, but actually, the seventh person never came.
So I only got to hear six stories..."{p}

"...The rest?
Let's see..."
While {f:I|I} was thinking it over, Hino leaned forward.{p}

"Yeah. It's a story about a doll.
He said that at this school, every year one person is offered up as a sacrifice to a doll.
And once this year's sacrifice is offered, the ritual of offering sacrifices to the doll comes to an end..."{p}

"{f:I'll|I'll} go check with the people I talked to yesterday!"
With that, {f:I|I} dashed out of the club room without even listening to Hino.
Were they all still around{f:, I wondered|, I wondered}?{p}

...Just as I thought.
Understandably, Iwashita had stayed home from school.
I'd better try someone else.{p}

{f:I|I} whirled around, startled.
The memory of my walk home yesterday had come flooding back{f:.|.}
There was no one behind {f:me|me}.{p}

Kazama had vanished partway through, after finishing his story.
Suddenly, like smoke.
I couldn't believe he had really disappeared for good, so I headed for Kazama's classroom.{p}

"Aaah!"
There stood a giant cockroach...
Yeah, right. There's no way something like that exists{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} pulled off the tasteless mask shaped like a giant cockroach.{p}

Kazama's smirking face emerged from inside the cockroach.
"Ahaha... You're as {f:boring|cute} as ever, you know.
{f:At this rate,|Sorry} {f:you'll never be a hit with the girls like I am.|for scaring you.}
{f:And here I was,|I know!} {f:going to teach you how to get girls.|To make it up to you, I'll take you somewhere nice next time.}"
Talking with this guy always throws me off.{p}

"{f:I know.|Okay?}
{f:As a special favor,|Let's go on a date.} {f:I'll teach you a gag that'll make the girls love you.|I'm sure it'll be fun.}
{f:Right now|Let's see...} {f:it's a special bargain, just five thousand yen.|How about this Sunday?}
{f:So,|Of course,} {f:how about one?|you'll say okay, right?}"{p}

When I went to Fukuzawa's classroom, she was happily chatting with a few other girls.
When {f:I|I} waved, she noticed and waved back.
Then she came trotting over.{p}

"What's up, {c}{f:|}?
Oh, did you just miss me that much?"
"Never mind that, this is serious{f:.|.}
Yesterday {f:we|we} definitely heard Arai's story{f:, right?|, didn't we?}"{p}

When I went to Hosoda's classroom, a few students were still there.
"Um, excuse me, is Hosoda here?"
When {f:I|I} asked no one in particular, they all burst out laughing loudly.{p}

{f:Huh|Whaaat}?
Does Hosoda really like toilets that much{f:?|?}
{f:Oh well|Oh well}.
{f:Guess I'll check the toilets|I'll try looking in the toilets}.{p}

...Hold on, wait a {f:sec|second}.
That's right{f:.|.} When I got home yesterday, for some reason I got a phone call from Hosoda{f:.|.}
I was wondering what it was about when he suddenly started talking about Takeuchi.
Yes, the story of Takeuchi, who never goes to the toilet.
Saying he wanted me to be the only one to hear this, he started telling me something strange{f:.|.}
That the story he told everyone was actually a lie.
That there's no such person as Takeuchi.{p}

{f:Apparently Hosoda had gotten|Hosoda told me he'd gotten} hold of a drink called Sanbura tea abroad, and he drinks it all the time.
Sanbura tea... drink it, and you never have to go to the toilet again.
He said he'd just told everyone a story he dreamed up while drinking that tea{f:.|.}
He also said some nonsense about letting me have a taste of it as a special treat...
Then why on earth is Hosoda going to the toilet{f:?|?}
Wasn't he supposed to have stopped needing the toilet{f:?|?}
{f:No|No}... maybe he didn't go there to relieve himself.{p}

I hear some people make a daily habit of reading the newspaper on the toilet.
Hosoda must just like the toilet as a place{f:.|.}
And that phone call might have been a joke.
{f:Whoa|Oh}, I don't have time to think about pointless stuff{f:!|.}
I have to find out about Arai...{p}

"Uh, um... Hosoda.
Never mind that, there's something important I need to talk to you about.
Do you remember Arai's doll story?"{p}

I'd try looking for Kiyose.
Then I should be able to tell whether what Hino said was just a joke or the truth{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} headed for Class 3-F, the one Hino had mentioned.{p}

...So Kiyose did exist.
And he hadn't come to yesterday's gathering.
{f:I|I} bowed to Kiyose once more and left Class 3-F.{p}

From what everyone said, {f:sure enough|just as I thought}, Arai had been there at that time, in that place, and told that doll story{f:.|. That's what it all pointed to.}
But Hino hadn't invited Arai.
The one Hino invited was Kiyose, who came down with a fever and couldn't make it.
...What on earth {f:is going on|does this mean}?
Who is Arai, {f:anyway|I wonder}?
Should I find out{f:?|?}{p}Or should I just forget about all this{f:?|?}

Fighting down the chill creeping up my spine, {f:I|I} went around the second-year classrooms one by one.
{f:After all|Because}, after hearing that story, {f:I|I} had seen something eerie that I couldn't explain{f:.|.}
If Arai's story {f:was|was} true, this year's sacrifice might be {f:me|me}.
Why had Arai, who wasn't supposed to exist, come to the newspaper club uninvited and told that story{f:?|?}{p}

"Shindo!"
I turned around, and there stood Shindo.
"{f:You came lookin' for Arai to beat the crap outta him, right|You seen Arai around anywhere}?
{f:Me too.|I'm lookin' for him so I can beat the crap outta him.}"
{f:I hadn't exactly planned to beat him up, but|Shindo} {f:I had come looking for him, just like Shindo.|was scary.}
{f:Somehow,|Besides,} {f:Shindo seemed a little pale.|he seemed a little pale somehow.}{p}

Shindo drew {f:me|me} into the shadow of a pillar.
Then he began to speak in a low voice.
It seemed to be something nobody else should overhear.{p}

...I can't stop thinking about the last thing he said.
One of us is gonna be this year's sacrifice.
And the guy who said that doesn't even exist in this world. Doesn't that creep you out?{p}

If this goes on, the doll will surely never leave {f:my|my} side for even a moment, and it will haunt {f:me|me} to death{f:.|.}
With each new sighting of the doll, I {f:could feel|can feel} {f:myself|myself} losing all will.
I can't shake the feeling that the doll is draining my life force little by little.
I miss the days when I tried to fight the doll, even knowing it was futile resistance{f:.|.}
But doing that {f:is|is} pointless.
The doll can't be touched{f:.|.}
Whenever {f:I|I} try to touch the doll, it vanishes instantly and reappears somewhere else.{p}

Expressionless as it was, it seemed to be sneering at {f:me|me}.
School had long since ended, and summer vacation had begun.
How much longer can {f:I|I} stay alive{f:?|, I wonder?}
Cursing Hino, wishing I'd never taken on that project, is ancient history now{f:.|.}
I don't feel like resenting anyone anymore.
{f:I|I}'d even stopped caring what that being called Arai really was.
Am {f:I|I} just going to die like this{f:?|?}
Should I try relying, just a little, on what scraps of willpower I still have left{f:?|?}{p}

...Come to think of it, ever since I left the house, the doll hadn't left {f:my|my} side.
Maybe it was watching {f:me|me}; it felt like the gap between it and {f:me|me} was slowly closing.
Did that mean the end was {f:near|near}?{p}

{f:I|I} didn't have any time {f:left|left}.
There was no room to {f:hesitate|hesitate} here.
{f:I|I} turned the knob and opened the heavy wooden door.{p}

...No {f:good|good}.
It was locked.
It was sturdily made, and there was no way I could break it open.{p}

November 14.
The doll arrived, but it looks nothing like Shoji.
I have decided to have it made again.{p}

December 18.
I have asked doll maker after doll maker and had every kind of doll made, but none of them satisfies me.
What I want is a perfect doll.{p}

"...Welcome."
Standing beyond the door was the man from the portrait.
It was the {f:principal|principal}.{p}

He was gripping a golf club in his hand.
"...Principal."
{f:I|I} murmured it without thinking.{p}

There was definitely something in there.
{f:I|I} shoved my hand into my pocket.
The key that had been tucked inside that {f:diary.|diary...}
That {f:had to|had to} be the key to this wardrobe.{p}

{f:This thing|This thing} was alive{f:.|, wasn't it?}
Between its brown skin and the yellow-green membrane ran a web of red and blue things like blood vessels, and from its smashed-open head it was feebly spewing a blackish liquid.
When I happened to look around, the doll that had been beside {f:me|me} until a moment ago was gone.
...I see.
So {f:this thing|this} was its true body{f:.|, then.}
The doll that was always at {f:my|my} side must have been {f:its|its} phantom{f:.|.}
And {f:this thing had kept growing inside this wardrobe|it had kept growing inside this wardrobe}, sucking out the soul of one sacrifice every year{f:.|.}
{f:My God...|Oh my God...}{p}

"Gyaaah!"
I couldn't tell what had happened, but the principal's chest split open and red blood gushed out of it like a fountain.
And that blood, of all things, was being sucked into a single point in midair{f:!|.}{p}

"...I-it's not me.
Th-the sacrifice is... that one..."
The principal pointed feebly toward {f:me|me}, {f:but|but} it was far too late for that to change anything.{p}

I could hardly breathe.
{f:My|My} heart was pounding so hard it felt like it would leap out of my mouth.
...It was over.
{f:I|I} was saved{f:.|, wasn't I?}
I didn't have to become the doll's sacrifice after all{f:.|!}{p}

The doll's face looked not unlike Shoji Arai's.
...{f:My God|Oh my God}.
If the contract is over, that means {f:this thing|this} comes back to life{f:!|, doesn't it!}
Bloody froth gurgled from {f:the thing's|the doll's} crooked-toothed mouth, and it cackled, its eyes unfocused.{p}

{f:I|I} reached for the diary and tore its pages to shreds.
I couldn't shake the feeling that this diary was wrapped in a black aura{f:.|.}
All I could rely on now was my own hunch{f:.|.}{p}

"Kiiiiiiiiih★"
...It seemed {f:my|my} hunch had been right{f:.|.}
The doll let out an agonized shriek, then stopped moving.
The yellow-green membrane covering the doll's surface melted and ran down {f:my|my} shoulder.
It gave off a tremendous stench, like rotting food scraps{f:, but|, but} {f:I|I} didn't have the energy left to care.{p}

It was densely covered in letters I had never seen before, and near the bottom someone had pressed a red fingerprint seal.
A seal in blood, no doubt{f:.|.}
This must be the contract with the devil{f:.|.}
Now that it was torn in two, had this contract lost its power{f:?|?}
If so, that would be {f:fine|good}...{p}

The stench finally became too much to bear, and {f:I|I} stood up.
How would this incident be dealt with{f:?|?}
Would the police just write it off as the principal having gone missing{f:?|?}{p}

{f:I|I}'m fully recovered now, ready for the second term that starts tomorrow.
Now {f:I|I} wonder.
Why did Shoji Arai join {f:our|our} gathering?{p}

Maybe, deep down, he never wanted to come back to life{f:?|?}
Sometimes that selfish, all-too-convenient thought crosses {f:my|my} mind.
Whatever the case, {f:it's|it's all} over.
I still doubt whether that thing was really the true form of the monster nesting in our school{f:, but|, but} at any rate, there will be no more victims of the doll{f:.|.}
That's {f:some|some} small comfort, at least.
...{f:I|I} still have nightmares about the doll.{p}

With that, Hosoda went home.
Everyone else trailed out after him.
"Good work, everyone~"{p}

The last of them left, and {f:I|I} checked that everything was locked up.
{f:I|I} kept replaying Arai's words in my head.
That's {f:right|right}, a story like that is just a lie{f:.|, isn't it.}
Someone here is going to die?
There's no way something that stupid could {f:happen...|happen!}{p}

"{f:No|Nah}, {f:I|I}'ll go home by myself{f:.|.}
I still have to return the key to the night-duty room{f:.|.}
I'd feel bad making you tag along just for that{f:...|, you know...}"{p}

{f:I|I} lied to Fukuzawa.
Actually, one of the seniors had made a copy of the newspaper club room key{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} was borrowing it at the moment{f:, so|, so} I didn't really need to return this key at all{f:.|, you see.}
To be frank, Fukuzawa is {f:the noisy type, so I|kind of loud, so I}'m not too comfortable around her{f:.|.}
Still, she's better than Iwashita.{p}

"See you then."
{f:We|We} set off in different directions.
...What do I do? This has turned into a real pain{f:.|.}
If I don't stall a little before heading over, she'll think something's strange.
I should have just dropped the stubbornness and said I'd go with her.
It can't be helped. I'll take the long way around.{p}

The school at night was unbelievably frightening.
I didn't want to remember, but everyone's stories from earlier kept surfacing in my head.
My eyes were gradually getting used to the dark, but a hallway lit only by emergency lights was {f:unnerving|unnerving}.{p}

{f:I|I} stopped in my tracks without thinking.
What do I do?
{f:It|It} seemed to be watching {f:me|me} intently{f:.|.}
I could feel greasy sweat seeping out over {f:my|my} hands and feet.
What's more, as if it had run out of patience with my not moving, {f:it started toward me|it started toward me}.{p}

Hopping, its body twisting, jerking along...
Against the green glow of the emergency lights, it kept coming closer and closer.
I had to get away from here, fast!{p}

{f:I|I} turned my back on {f:the thing|the figure} and ran at full speed.
All I could think about was getting away from {f:it|the figure}.
But no matter how hard I ran, {f:its|the figure's} footsteps never grew any fainter.
Ah, that's Fukuzawa walking over there{f:!|!}
{f:I|I} ran as hard as I could, my legs nearly tangling.{p}

"...{c}{f:|}.
{c}{f:|}!"
Fukuzawa had pried {f:me|me} off her back and was shaking my shoulders.{p}

"What's wrong★
You're drenched in sweat.
Did you return the key already?"{p}

{f:No|No}, I'll just keep going straight ahead{f:.|.}
That figure was just my imagination{f:.|.}
{f:Fukuzawa and I|Fukuzawa and I} kept walking straight on.{p}

Then the figure abruptly vanished around the corner.
...It didn't vanish. It was an illusion{f:.|.}
Thank goodness, it was just {f:my|my} imagination after all{f:.|.}
Then we turned the last corner.{p}

"{c}{f:|}, you sure walk fast."
Fukuzawa said.
{f:I|I} didn't answer her and kept walking.
That thing seemed to be staring at {f:my|my} back{f:.|.}
It didn't look like it was going to follow {f:me|me}{f:.|.}
At this hour{f:,|,} of course, the students' entrance was locked.
So we'd have to go out through the side gate{f:.|...}{p}

Fukuzawa looked at {f:me|me} and laughed.
...Wait {f:a second|a minute}, what's that sound?
I could definitely hear something.{p}

{f:I|I} looked back behind me.
The glow of the streetlights shone faintly in through the windows.
Something flickered in and out of view.{p}

Fukuzawa was shaking {f:my|my} shoulders.
"What's wrong?
You're drenched in sweat."{p}

I'd better not ask after all{f:.|.}
{f:Right|Yes}, if I said something like that here, she'd be sure to think {f:my|my} head had gone funny.
I'd better not say anything{f:.|, right?}{p}

"Seriously, I wondered what was wrong with you back there.
Did something happen?"
Fukuzawa was still looking at {f:me|me} with concern.
"I'm fine{f:.|.}
I just got a little dizzy{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} have low blood pressure, so I get like this sometimes{f:.|.}
It's {f:a real pain|such a pain, huh}."
{f:I|I} came up with a plausible story and smoothed things over.{p}

{f:I|I} {f:cracked a joke right back|joked right back} at her.
That's {f:right|right}, let's get out of here, fast.
You never know what might happen in a school at night{f:.|.}
And so {f:we|we} hurried away from the school.{p}

{f:I|I} decided it was better not to dig any further into this matter.
I had a feeling that if I did, something terrible would happen, and honestly, I was scared.
{f:But|But} who was Arai, really{f:?|?}
{f:I|I} was wandering absently down the hallway beside the second-year classrooms.
"{a}!"
Startled by the voice calling to me, {f:I|I} turned around.{p}

.................................No, that's not it.
I could tell {f:my|my} body temperature was steadily dropping.
The doll was sucking the warmth out of {f:my|my} body{f:.|!}
My eyelids kept trying to close.
People get sleepy when their body temperature drops, don't they...
If I fell asleep like this, would I never wake up again{f:?|?}
The doll was no longer beside {f:me|me}.{p}

The doll was standing there, looking down at {f:me|me} as I lay on the bed.
It was looking at {f:me|me} and laughing.
Then, glancing back at {f:me|me}, it walked out of the room.
I see... so that school will finally be free of the doll's curse{f:.|.}
After it offers {f:me|me} up as its last sacrifice...
For some reason, the feelings I had already lost came back to me for an instant.{p}

Did that doll have feelings{f:?|?}
Maybe it had some fragment of feeling.
It couldn't be thinking nothing at all{f:.|.}
At the very least, it wanted to haunt {f:me|me} to death...
Maybe I could reach the doll, heart to heart.
With that thought, {f:I|I} decided to pour what little strength I had left into reaching the doll's heart.
I knew it was very dangerous{f:, though|, though}.
{f:I|I} lay down on the bed and slowly closed my eyes.{p}

.......................................
It didn't seem to answer {f:my|my} question{f:.|.}
I asked once more.
Something echoed inside {f:my|my} head.
It was the sound of a man sobbing{f:.|.}{p}

When I opened my eyes, the doll was no longer there.
What on earth had that doll been saying{f:?|?}
What had it been trying to tell me{f:...|...}
{f:I|I} remembered Arai's story.{p}

How cruel...
In the end, nobody cares about anything that doesn't concern them{f:.|.}
And I bet they're all relieved that they weren't the ones sacrificed.{p}

{f:I|I} was so frustrated.
Tears ran down my cheeks.
The tears were warm...
Even someone like me could still shed warm tears{f:.|.}
Then it hit {f:me|me}.
{f:I|I} didn't want to die yet.
There were still so many things I wanted to do before I died{f:.|.}
At that thought, the feeling that I had to do something welled up out of my apathy.
Just then, {f:I|I} suddenly remembered Arai's story.{p}

Whatever I do, it's wasted effort{f:.|.}
How many people before me have struggled in vain{f:?|?}
No, the ones who were chosen probably never even felt the will to try{f:.|.}
I don't care anymore. Everything can just stay the way it is.{p}

{f:I|I} didn't go in.
I still held a faint hope that the doll might be nothing but an illusion{f:.|.}
In the midst of these unreal events, common sense had begun to get in the way.
And so {f:I|I} turned to go home.{p}

"Principal..."
Oh, no{f:.|.}
Of course he'd have a key to his own office{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} dashed over to the cabinet on the spot.{p}

Then a figure flitted past the window.
(Arai...? {f:No, it's just my imagination|No, it's just my imagination})
{f:I|I} turned away.{p}

(You'll take over the contract.
If the contract isn't completed, {f:I|I} can't go back, you see.)
I looked toward the school building.{p}

There was a figure standing outside the front entrance.
(You know what happens if you don't keep the contract.
But whatever you wish for will be yours.){p}

The figure vanished.
No one's there. It's just my imagination{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} felt relieved.
When I reached into my pocket to wipe the sweat running down my forehead, I found a scrap of paper in it.{p}

First, {f:I|I} checked the cabinet.
The glass-fronted cabinet was crammed with all kinds of certificates and trophies.
So this was the glory bought in exchange for sacrifices{f:...|...}
Somehow {f:I|I} felt a tightness in my chest.
It was because these tokens of that glory felt terribly small for something paid for with human lives{f:.|.}
The cabinet was firmly locked in four places{f:,|,} and there was nothing I could do.
If I wanted to open it, it looked like I'd have to break the glass{f:.|.}
Maybe I'd better look somewhere else{f:.|.}{p}

{f:I|I} decided to check the desk drawers.
I'd open them in order from the bottom.
It was a single-pedestal desk with three drawers.
The bottom one... held documents that {f:I|I} couldn't make heads or tails of.
{f:Now|Next}, the second one{f:.|.}
There were lots of business card holders...
Mixed in with the cards of big shots I'd never heard of were cards from girls at some clubs and hostess bars.
So even the principal goes to places like that{f:.|.}
{f:Teachers are human too, I guess|...Somehow}, {f:so maybe he goes there now and then to blow off steam|I just can't picture it}.{p}

{f:...Wait, no|But this has nothing to do with anything}, {f:this is no time to be impressed|I need to check other places too}.
Now, the top drawer{f:.|...}
Wh-what... It's no use{f:.|.}
It's locked.
It's built so sturdily, there's no way I could break it{f:.|.}

(Isn't there something I could use to open it{f:...|...})
I looked around the principal's office{f:,|,} but I didn't see anything.
({f:What do I do|What should I do}...)
As I thought that, {f:my|my} eyes fell on the chair.
I'm going to die anyway if this goes on{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} went over to the desk and lifted the chair.{p}

A loud crash rang out.
The noise must have carried all around{f:.|.}
I have to find something before {g}someone comes{f:.|.}{p}

"Help {f:me|me}!"
I ran down the stairs and kept running.
"Somebody! Help me!"{p}

I could see the faculty room.
If I get there, it'll be all right{f:.|.}
{f:I|I} opened the faculty room door.{p}

{f:I tried to run|I wanted to run} somewhere else, but where in this cramped space could I possibly go{f:?|?}
I glanced at the window.
The principal's office was on the third floor, so escaping through the window was impossible{f:.|.}
...I don't care what happens anymore!{p}

...But was this really the right thing to do{f:?|?}
Maybe there had been some better way.
...Not that it matters now.
Another new sacrifice will be added.
And {f:I|I} couldn't even stop it.{p}

It was covered with writing I had never seen before, and near the bottom a red seal had been pressed with a finger.
It must be a seal of blood{f:.|.}
This must be the devil's contract{f:.|.}{p}

{f:I|I} hurriedly tore the contract to pieces.
I could only hope that would strip it of its power{f:...|...}
The stench finally got to be too much, and {f:I|I} stood up.
{f:How would this whole incident be handled?|I wondered how this whole incident would be handled.}
Would the police just {f:write it off|write it off} as the principal having gone missing?
And what would the police make of the broken doll in the principal's office{f:?|...?}{p}

"Kiiiiiiieee!"
The doll let out an anguished shriek, and then it stopped moving.
The yellow-green slime that had coated the doll's surface melted and was running down {f:my|my} shoulders.
So this sand was the doll's weak point{f:.|.}
{f:Apparently|It seemed} a half-finished doll like this didn't stand a chance against the sand.
Half its head had already melted away.{p}

"I felt better, so I came in.
I really am sorry about yesterday."
"Never mind that. Yesterday, you met Arai, didn't you?"{p}

She gave me a pat on the back and strode briskly off.
I followed along behind her like a lackey.
And we went around the second-year classrooms, visiting them one by one.{p}

I went to talk it over with Shindo and Iwashita.
But we couldn't find any way out of this enormous maze.
And all I could do was go on living my everyday life.{p}

"Hey, {a}, get over here!"
I was spacing out during break when Shindo came running into my classroom.
And I followed Shindo, just like he told me to.{p}

A crowd had gathered in the schoolyard.
"What happened?"
"Fukuzawa just killed herself."{p}

Arai had appeared before the three of us...
Was it to tell us something?
Or was it to kill us, just like those two?{p}

No, I never want to go see Kazama again{f:.|.}
{f:Like hell I'm going.|There's no way I'm going.}
It'd be smarter to try someone else{f:.|, wouldn't it?}{p}

He seemed to be hiding something{f:.|.}
And that sudden fever of his sounded kind of fishy too{f:.|.}
So I went back to Class 3-F one more time.
On the way, I saw Kiyose through the window, running across the schoolyard.
{f:It looked like he was|He seemed to be} heading for the old school building.{p}

